# FASE 10 — Kryon-Qwen3-8B specialist candidate (alternativa a kryon-gpt-oss)
#
# Why this exists: 15 bench runs against THM Pyrat / Operation Endgame
# showed gpt-oss-20b ceils at 2-stage chains under output ambiguity
# (FASES 1-8 documentation). Qwen3-8B Thinking scored notably higher on
# the benchmarks that matter for agentic pentest:
#   - Tau2-Bench (multi-turn tool use): Qwen3.5-4B 79.9 vs gpt-oss-120b 67.8
#   - BFCL-v3 (function calling):       Qwen3 71.9 vs gpt-oss ~67-68
#   - GPQA Diamond (reasoning):         Qwen3 ~78 vs gpt-oss-20b ~71.5
# Trade-off: gpt-oss-20b wins AIME math (98.7 vs ~92) and has 131K
# context vs Qwen3's 33K — neither matters for our use case.
#
# Apache 2.0, ~5 GB VRAM at q4 (vs 11 GB for kryon-gpt-oss) — leaves
# 6+ GB free for parallel training/embedding/etc.

FROM qwen3:8b

# FASE 11.A — num_ctx 24K (sweet spot between 16K truncation vs 32K
# VRAM-ceiling). Empirically measured on RTX 5070 Ti Laptop 12 GB:
#
#   num_ctx  | model + KV cache  | headroom for embeddings + system
#   ---------|-------------------|----------------------------------
#   16K      | 7.8 GB            | 3.4 GB ✓ comfortable
#   24K      | ~9.0 GB           | 2.2 GB ✓ sweet spot (this row)
#   32K      | 10.8 GB           | 1.4 GB ⚠ tight (no second model)
#   65K YaRN | ~14 GB            | ❌ doesn't fit
#
# Important — what does NOT consume VRAM (common confusion):
#   - nuclei, sqlmap, nmap, curl, etc. are CPU/RAM Go/Python binaries,
#     zero GPU usage. They don't compete for this budget.
#   - nomic-embed-text DOES use VRAM (~600 MB) — counted in the
#     "headroom" column above.
#   - Hot-swapping a second model (e.g. compact-model for context
#     trimming) consumes its full footprint; the 2.2 GB headroom at
#     24K is just enough for a 3-4B Q4 model alongside.
#
# The Pyrat bench showed qwen3-8b @ 16K hitting <think> truncation
# around the 3rd tool call (forcing premature "Resumen Ejecutivo"
# exits). 24K is 1.5× the observed working set and leaves a second
# model + nomic-embed-text concurrent runs comfortable.
# Qwen3-8B native context is 32768 (no YaRN needed at this size).
PARAMETER num_ctx 24576
# FASE 11.A — num_predict 8K (doubled from 4096). The Pyrat bench
# showed qwen3-8b emitting 2-3K of <think> reasoning per turn; 4096
# was getting truncated mid-hypothesis, forcing the model to commit to
# half-formed plans. 8192 lets the thinking-mode pipeline fully render
# without truncation pressure.
PARAMETER num_predict 8192

# Temperature 0.3 — same rationale as kryon-gpt-oss (F179): agentic
# pentest needs reproducible findings, 0.3 keeps variance low while
# leaving enough diversity for alt-path exploration when a tool fails.
# Qwen3 thinking-mode default is 0.6; we override to match gpt-oss
# calibration so bench results are comparable.
PARAMETER temperature 0.3

# Qwen3-recommended sampling for thinking-mode reliability:
# top_p 0.95, top_k 20, min_p 0 (from Qwen3 model card).
PARAMETER top_p 0.95
PARAMETER top_k 20
PARAMETER min_p 0

# Qwen3 reasoning ON by default — thinking traces emit <think></think>
# tags that the SDK's reasoning parser picks up just like Harmony
# channels (validated F162 path works for both).
# To disable thinking for a specific call use ``/no_think`` in the
# system prompt or ``enable_thinking=False`` via the chat API.

# Stop tokens — Qwen3 native tokens (model card).
PARAMETER stop "<|im_end|>"
PARAMETER stop "<|endoftext|>"
